    "columns_1_N4QetX": {
      "type": "columns-1",
      "blocks": {
        "dropdown_MpQ7eL": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Retail Price Inclusions",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Pre-retreat:<br/>● 2 group Pod Unity/Community Calls led by Anne.<br/>● 2 group Conscious Breath group Calls led by Jillian.<br/><br/>Post-Retreat:<br/>​● 2 Group Pod Unity/Community Calls.<br/>● 1 Private Living the Dolphin Way Coaching call with Anne.<br/><br/>On-island program & activities<br/>● Morning grounding, intention setting, and heart-opening session.<br/>● Dolphin-guided meditations, energy transmissions, and intuitive teachings.<br/>● Breathwork sessions with Jillian to expand presence, relaxation, and flow.<br/>● Guided snorkeling & breath-hold diving practices (all levels welcome).<br/>● Daily boat trips to meet the dolphins (5 days out, weather permitting) in warm, clear Caribbean waters.<br/>● Evening community circles for reflection, sharing, and deepening.<br/>● Time to integrate, rest, and explore the beauty of Bimini.<br/><br/>Accommodations & logistics<br/>● All accommodations: 5 nights on Bimini + 1 night in Ft. Lauderdale.<br/>● Meals: All meals on the island except 1 dinner.<br/>● Airport transfers on Bimini upon Monday arrival and Saturday departure (with group travel).<br/>● Snorkel equipment provided.<br/>● Complimentary use of kayaks and bicycles.<br/>● Taxis to/from the one dinner at a local Bimini restaurant<br/>● Wi-Fi connection, where and when available<br/>● Drinking water & hot beverages<br/><br/>Dining Summary (what meals are included): <br/>● All meals are lovingly prepared for you on the island, except for one dinner out at a local restaurant. All dietary restrictions and requests can be accommodated.<br/><br/>Other options on your own:<br/>● Dolphin House - a unique home hand built by a local man dedicated to his love for the dolphins.<br/>● The Healing Hole - a local 'fountain of youth' in the mangroves.<br/>● Hemingway House - where Hemingway spent much time</p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#513589",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_ajAxaD": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Retail Price Exclusions",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>● Travel costs to and from Fort Lauderdale, Florida</p><p>● Flight costs to/from Bimini (approximately $632 - subject to change without prior notice)</p><p>● Two dinners, Sunday and Wednesday night & Breakfast on Monday</p><p>● Hotel and boat crew Gratuities 5-10% of the retreat cost (Customary)</p><p>● Ocean view room upgrade (Optional)</p><p>● All individual body work sessions. The cost is $120 for an hour (Optional)</p><p>● Retreat photos: $95 (optional and subject to change without prior notice)</p><p>● Travel Insurance (Highly recommended. Check out <a href=\"https://www.worldnomads.com/?affiliate=whlnddlphn&subId=weblink&utm_source=whlnddlphn&utm_medium=affiliate&utm_campaign=Affiliate&utm_content=weblink\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">World Nomads</span></a>.)</p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#513589",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_zxUc4t": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Reservation and Payment",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>● Down payment: $1,000 (Non-refundable)</p><p>● Balance due by: March 1, 2026</p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#513589",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_F3F9mP": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Cancellation and Rescheduling of Booking",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>● Full refunds are available within 7 days of purchase.</p><p>● After 7 days, payments are non-refundable. If the retreat is full, and we can fill your spot, you may transfer your payment to another retreat within one year.</p><p><strong>If you need to cancel, please email us. Your cancellation is only valid once you receive a confirmation email from us.</strong></p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#513589",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_aMTFHh": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Waiver of Responsibility",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>By signing up for this Retreat, you agree to all Terms, Deposit Conditions, and this Waiver. In making this booking, you acknowledge and understand the extent of this agreement, and hereby release, absolve, and hold harmless the retreat organizers, their directors, leaders, guides, facilitators, captains, crew, volunteers, and any other parties connected with the retreat, individually or collectively, from any liability for injury, misadventure, harm, loss, inconvenience, or damage sustained while participating in any aspect of this retreat experience.</p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#513589",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_Ypd9Wp": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Changes To the Program",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Mother Nature – the weather and the Dolphins – are not under our control, and sometimes it may be necessary to make changes to the program, accommodations or boat. We are not responsible for any consequences arising from such changes, cancellations or delays of programs. In particular, failure to see particular species of wildlife will not be a breach of contract on our part. </p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#513589",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_rzQq4A": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Insurance",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>We highly recommend that all participants obtain travel insurance. Travel Insured International offers insurance for trip cost, trip cancellation & interruption, and pays for loss due to unforeseen circumstance, death, injury, or illness to you or a member of your family. It also includes coverage for missed connections due to weather, pays for lost deposits due to the financial default of the airline, the tour operator, or cruise line. It pays for baggage delays, travel delays, medical expenses and emergency assistance.</p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#513589",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        }
      },
